# radroots_nostr_runtime

`radroots_nostr_runtime` is a private, publication-frozen predecessor package.
Its former client/runtime integration is no longer active by default and must
not receive new consumers. Final relay I/O belongs to
`radroots_transport_nostr`; final source/sink orchestration belongs to
`radroots_sync`.

## Compatibility quarantine

The private `radroots_nostrdb` runtime adapter still resolves the predecessor
sink types behind an opt-in, non-default feature. `RCRV1-DEV-010` therefore
retains this documentation-hidden, `publish = false` package only until the
sync-orchestration cutover. Step 215 removes the package and the adapter after
their behavior is owned by `radroots_sync`.

Do not add consumers, features, public contracts, or runtime behavior here.
The remaining opt-in source is also governed by `RCRV1-DEV-007` and cannot
enter a release feature closure.

## Overview

 * runtime builder, runtime events, and long-lived connection state types;
 * subscription specifications, policies, handles, and traffic-light status
   models;
 * sink abstractions and snapshot types used by higher-level network
   orchestration;
 * quarantined feature-gated predecessor integration retained only for the
   governed removal gate.

